module

public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteLocallyFreeCoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteLocallyFreeModulePullback
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FiniteTypeQuasicoherentExtension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.Perfect.ResolutionProperty
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentCartesianOnAffineCharts
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.QuasicoherentPushforwardQcqs

/-!
# Covering sections of a direct image by a finite locally free module on the target

Let `f : X ⟶ Y` be a quasi-compact and quasi-separated morphism of algebraic spaces over a
scheme `S`, with `Y` quasi-compact, quasi-separated and carrying the resolution property of
Stacks 0GUS, and let `ℱ` be a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module.  This file proves the step of the
proof of Stacks 0GUU — and of Stacks 0GUT, of which Stacks 0GUU is the case `ℒ = 𝒪_X` — which
turns finitely many sections of the direct image `f_*ℱ` over an affine étale chart of `Y` into a
finite locally free `𝒪_Y`-module mapping to `f_*ℱ` through them, and then into a finite locally
free `𝒪_X`-module mapping to `ℱ`.

In the notation of the source, `ℋ_n = f_*(ℱ ⊗ ℒ^{⊗ n})`, the `s_i` are sections of `ℋ_{-n_i}`
over the chart `V`, and the step is the sentence *"Suppose we can find finite locally free
`𝒪_Y`-modules `ℰ_i` and maps `ℰ_i → ℋ_{-n_i}` such that `s_i` is in the image"* together with
the two sentences that follow it.  Here `f_*ℱ` is quasi-coherent by Stacks 03M9, a finite type
quasi-coherent submodule of it containing the given sections over `V` exists by Stacks 0829, and
the resolution property of `Y` covers that submodule by a finite locally free module.
Transposing along `f^* ⊣ f_*` and pulling back finite local freeness gives the map on `X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_finiteLocallyFree_epi_submodule_modulePushforward`: the finite
  locally free `𝒪_Y`-module `ℰ` and the epimorphism onto a submodule of `f_*ℱ` whose sections
  over the chart contain the given ones.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_finiteLocallyFree_modulePullback_hom_of_hasResolutionProperty`:
  the same, together with the pullback `f^*ℰ`, which is again finite locally free, and the map
  `f^*ℰ ⟶ ℱ` transposing `ℰ ⟶ f_*ℱ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.isQuasicoherentOnSite_of_isFiniteLocallyFreeOnSite`: a finite locally
  free module is quasi-coherent.

## Implementation notes

**The image of `ℰ ⟶ f_*ℱ`.**  The source asks for the sections `s_i` to lie in the image of the
map from `ℰ`.  The image is produced here as a submodule `𝒢` of `f_*ℱ` through which the map
factors by an epimorphism: `𝒢` is the finite type quasi-coherent submodule supplied by
Stacks 0829, and the epimorphism onto it is the one the resolution property of `Y` produces, so
the image of the composite `ℰ ⟶ 𝒢 ⟶ f_*ℱ` is `𝒢` itself.  Membership of the `s_i` is then
membership in `𝒢` over the chart.

**Which form of Stacks 0829 is used.**  Not the colimit assertion but the étale extension
property `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartExtensionProperty` underlying it, in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartExtensionProperty_id` together with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartExtensionProperty.exists_forall_mem`, which encloses finitely many
prescribed sections over one affine chart in a single finite type quasi-coherent submodule.
Its output is a `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartSubmodule`, read as a submodule of `f_*ℱ` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartSubmodule.toSubmodule`, finite type on the site by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartSubmodule.isFiniteTypeOnSite_toSubmodule` and quasi-coherent by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ChartSubmodule.isCartesianOnAffineCharts_toSubmodule` with Descent,
Proposition 03DX (2).

**The hypotheses on `f`.**  Quasi-compactness and quasi-separatedness of `f` are what Stacks 03M9
asks of it, and they are weaker than the affineness or quasi-affineness of Stacks 0GUU.  What is
**not** proved here is the remaining content of Stacks 0GUU: that the transposed map
`f^*ℰ ⟶ ℱ` is an epimorphism.  That needs the two transports the source performs on the chart —
that a finite type quasi-coherent module on the quasi-affine scheme `V ×_Y X` is generated by
finitely many global sections (Properties, Proposition 01Q3 (8) in the form
`AlgebraicGeometry.hasResolutionProperty_of_isAmple` uses it), and that local surjectivity of a
map of `𝒪_X`-modules may be tested after base change to that chart — neither of which is a
statement of this file.

**The module universe.**  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePushforward` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.modulePullback` are defined at the universe `u` of the schemes, so the
resolution property of `Y` is used at `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.HasResolutionProperty.{u, u}`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GUU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GUU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GUT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GUT)
